## API Patterns

### URL Convention
```
/api/{resource}              ← plural, kebab-case
/api/{resource}/my-{resource} ← user-scoped
/api/{resource}/:id/{action}  ← actions
/api/procurement/{sub-resource} ← nested
```

### CRITICAL: Route Ordering
Static routes MUST come before parameterized routes:
```js
router.get("/my-logs/export", ...);  // FIRST: static
router.put("/my-logs/:id", ...);     // THEN: parameterized
router.get("/my-logs", ...);         // THEN: static
router.get("/:id", ...);             // LAST: catch-all param
```

### Response Format
```js
// Success: { success: true, data: {...}, message: "..." }
// Error: { message: "Descriptive error message" }
// List: { items: [...], pagination: { total, page, limit, pages } }
```

### Controller Pattern
```js
export const fn = async (req, res) => {
  try {
    // req.user set by protect middleware
    // Validate → Query → Authorize → Mutate → Notify → Respond
    res.status(200).json({ message: "Success", data: result });
  } catch (error) {
    res.status(500).json({ message: "Server error", error: error.message });
  }
};
```

