## Frontend/Backend Structure Conventions

### State Management
- **NO Redux, Zustand, or any state library**
- Global state: 3 Context providers only (Auth, Notification, Company)
- Feature data: local `useState` + API calls
- `useAuth()` for user/role; `useNotifications()` for notifications

### Two Axios Instances (important!)
- `frontend/src/services/api.js` — primary (60s timeout)
- `frontend/src/api/axios.js` — secondary (30s timeout)
- Check which one the existing module uses before adding calls

### Component Pattern
```jsx
const Page = () => {
  const { user } = useAuth();
  const canWrite = ['admin', 'superadmin'].includes(user?.role);
  const [items, setItems] = useState([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  
  useEffect(() => { fetchItems(); }, []);
  
  return <Container fluid className="py-4">...</Container>;
};
export default Page;
```

### UI Library
- Bootstrap 5.3 + React-Bootstrap 2.9 ONLY
- Icons: `react-icons/fa` ONLY
- No Tailwind, no MUI, no Ant Design

